{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013tsesZQXPUfAU4mo9pfo4T","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61a2af5c-d600-4497-9e1f-4081c4861a6a","uuid":"fd397771-9580-4a53-8a70-56518548ce6e","timestamp":"2026-06-10T17:58:54.737Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- **sos_57**: \"amount of mana spent\" recorded at cast time as","newString":"- **sos_201**: miracle is card-local on `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`; \"first card\n  drawn this turn\" uses the engine's existing `cards_drawn_this_turn`, which\n  was tracked but never reset — added a reset at turn rollover in\n  `GameState.advance_phase` (nothing else reads the field). Miracle cost {2}\n  is paid from the pool, then the spell is put on the stack via\n  `cast_spell_free` from hand. No prompt is offered when the cost can't be\n  paid. Engine limitation: pools empty every phase and the priority loop\n  doesn't enumerate mana abilities, so in a fully-driven turn a miracle needs\n  mana already floating when the trigger resolves.\n- **sos_57**: \"amount of mana spent\" recorded at cast time as","originalFile":"# Key decisions log\n\n- **E1**: TODO said to fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` only in `cast_spell`. Also\n  fired it in `cast_spell_free` — casting without paying mana is still casting\n  (rule 601.2), and sos_226/sos_257 triggers must see free casts (e.g. spells\n  cast off sos_1/sos_120). Copies made via `copy_spell` still never fire it.\n- **sos_1**: `AttacksTriggeredEvent` existed (FDN cards register on it) but the\n  engine never fired it; added the fire in `declare_attackers_step` after all\n  attackers are declared (rule 508.4). Additive; no existing test registers\n  attack triggers through combat, so no behavior change elsewhere.\n- **sos_1**: \"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\"\n  — `move_to_zone` only consulted replacements for battlefield exits. Added a\n  `SpellToGraveyardReplacementEvent` (subclass of MoveToGraveyard…) passed by\n  `_resolve_spell` for instants/sorceries, and extended `move_to_zone` to\n  consult replacements for stack exits too. Replacement is one-shot, keyed on\n  the specific spell object. Limitation: a counterspell that bins the card\n  directly (fdn_48-style `_counter_spell`) bypasses move_to_zone and isn't\n  intercepted.\n- **sos_1**: per TODO, when exactly one legal graveyard target exists the\n  trigger auto-selects it (no prompt); the \"may\" decline is only offered via\n  `choose_card` returning None when there are 2+ candidates.\n- **sos_257**: restricted mana is a per-type count inside `ManaPool`\n  (`add_restricted` + optional `spell=` param on `can_pay`/`pay`, threaded\n  through `cast_spell`). Only one restriction kind exists\n  (instant/sorcery-only) — deliberate single-card limitation. Restricted mana\n  is treated as spent first when eligible.\n- **sos_257**: animation mutates the card in place and updates\n  `_original_card_types` so `EffectManager.apply_all` resets don't undo it\n  (the effect has no duration). The pump is a normal Layer-7c until-EOT\n  continuous effect; `apply_all` is invoked after adding so it is immediately\n  observable. Animated land is not summoning sick (per plan note). If the\n  animated land left and re-entered the battlefield it would stay a creature —\n  accepted edge, not reachable in these tests.\n- **Ability activation in tests**: the engine has no index-addressed\n  `ActivateAbility` helper; the real activation path is\n  `engine.abilities.activate_ability` over `get_*_abilities()[index]` wrapped\n  in `ActivatedAbilityInstance`. Tests drive abilities that way.\n- **sos_120**: TODO suggested `copy_spell` for the Paradigm copy, but\n  `copy_spell` copies never count as *cast* and the spec says \"you may CAST a\n  copy of it from exile\". Implemented as an actual card copy placed in exile\n  and cast via `cast_spell_free` (fires the cast event, can be responded to).\n  A resolved copy ceases to exist (rule 707.10a): its replacement removes it\n  from the stack zone with `prevented=True` instead of redirecting. The\n  recurring main-phase trigger is registered once per (controller, name) —\n  later resolutions of same-named spells only get the self-exile clause.\n- **sos_13**: rule 722.3c (in this workspace's RULEBOOK) settles the cost\n  question: the prepared copy is created in exile *when the permanent becomes\n  prepared* and is cast by *paying* {W} (no free-cast wording, unlike\n  Paradigm's 702.192a). Implemented the cast as an activated ability whose\n  cost pays {W} and whose effect casts the copy from exile (the engine has no\n  pay-and-cast-from-exile entry point). The copy ceases to exist when it\n  resolves (707.10a) or when the Emeritus leaves the battlefield / unprepares\n  (722.3c).\n- **sos_13**: self-ETB effects must run inline in `register_triggers`\n  (fdn_106 pattern): the engine fires `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`\n  *before* calling the entering card's `register_triggers`, so a self-ETB\n  `TriggerRegistration` never fires (verified empirically with fdn_235).\n  \"Target player\" for the Inkling token is chosen by the controller at\n  resolution via `choose`, the engine's pattern for trigger targets.\n- **sos_57**: \"amount of mana spent\" recorded at cast time as\n  `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` in `cast_spell` (after reductions; X\n  treated as 0) and `0` in `cast_spell_free` — the pool doesn't track per-spell\n  totals. Ambiguity: whether \"if you control a Wizard\" is checked on resolution\n  or when the delayed trigger fires — followed TODO: checked when the delayed\n  trigger fires (one-shot, then unregistered). Engine limitation: only\n  precombat mains fire the E2 event, so \"your next main phase\" = your next\n  precombat main.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":57,"oldLines":6,"newStart":57,"newLines":15,"lines":["   `TriggerRegistration` never fires (verified empirically with fdn_235).","   \"Target player\" for the Inkling token is chosen by the controller at","   resolution via `choose`, the engine's pattern for trigger targets.","+- **sos_201**: miracle is card-local on `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`; \"first card","+  drawn this turn\" uses the engine's existing `cards_drawn_this_turn`, which","+  was tracked but never reset — added a reset at turn rollover in","+  `GameState.advance_phase` (nothing else reads the field). Miracle cost {2}","+  is paid from the pool, then the spell is put on the stack via","+  `cast_spell_free` from hand. No prompt is offered when the cost can't be","+  paid. Engine limitation: pools empty every phase and the priority loop","+  doesn't enumerate mana abilities, so in a fully-driven turn a miracle needs","+  mana already floating when the trigger resolves."," - **sos_57**: \"amount of mana spent\" recorded at cast time as","   `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` in `cast_spell` (after reductions; X","   treated as 0) and `0` in `cast_spell_free` — the pool doesn't track per-spell"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
